 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Audition Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an audition form?\", \"a\": \"An audition form is what a performer fills in before trying out for a part. Merriam-Webster defines an audition as a trial performance to appraise an entertainer's merits. The form tells the panel who is performing, which roles they want, and which rehearsal dates they cannot make.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the parts you are filling and every rehearsal date, then describe them in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form with its time slots, plus a database of every sign-up. Send the link to two past performers as a test before you post the casting notice.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an audition form template include?\", \"a\": \"Start with contact details, the roles a performer wants, past experience, and every rehearsal date they cannot make. Add a headshot and resume upload for acting roles and a vocal range question for singers. If you begin from an audition form pdf, carry its questions into your prompt and leave its layout behind.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an audition form close automatically at the deadline?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you build it that way. Tell Emergent the closing date and time, and the form stops taking sign-ups at that moment and shows a closed message instead. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/giveaway'>giveaway landing page</a> uses the same kind of cutoff, where entries stop at a set time.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I let performers book time slots on an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Enter when the first slot starts and how long each one runs, and the form offers each performer only the times still open. Add a waitlist as well. Once the last slot goes, later sign-ups join the waitlist and get an email when a time frees up.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I collect self-tapes with an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Ask for a link to the self-tape and the role it is for, and have the field accept only a web address. A link keeps the form quick to fill in on a phone, and the video stays wherever the actor posted it. The panel opens each tape from the sign-up list.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an audition form ask for a headshot and resume?\", \"a\": \"For acting roles, yes. Ask for both as uploads and store them on the performer's record, the way a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/rental-application'>rental application form</a> keeps pay stubs with each application. For an orchestra or choir, ask for a recording link instead, since the panel judges the sound.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send callbacks from audition form responses?\", \"a\": \"Mark each performer as a callback on the response list, and the app emails every callback the time and the scene to prepare. Performers who are not called back can get a separate, kinder note the same day. Emergent builds both emails from your prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should audition forms be?\", \"a\": \"Short enough to finish on a phone in about 5 minutes. Put each topic on its own screen, and show the singing and dance questions only to people who pick those roles. Forms Emergent builds have no response caps, even for a large open call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do judges score auditions from the form?\", \"a\": \"Give every judge the same criteria, such as tone and timing, each scored from 1 to 10 on their own screen. Ask for a one-line note with each score, which helps when two performers tie. The panel's sheet is an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/assessment'>assessment form</a> with a fixed rubric, tied to each sign-up.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build an audition form that saves every response to a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build an audition form that saves every response to a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Role Selection\", \"add\": \"Add a role selection list that shows singers a vocal range question.\"}, {\"label\": \"Conflict Calendar\", \"add\": \"Add a conflict calendar where each performer ticks the rehearsal dates they cannot make.\"}, {\"label\": \"Headshot Upload\", \"add\": \"Add a headshot upload and a resume upload saved to each performer's record.\"}, {\"label\": \"Judge Scoring\", \"add\": \"Add judge scoring from 1 to 10, averaged across the panel.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
